# Endpoint Security (OWASP max)

Apply on **every** endpoint in every microservice — no exceptions for “read-only” routes.

## Baseline (every response)

Set security headers via shared middleware/helper from `packages/shared` (one place), not copy-pasted per handler:

- `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload`
- `Content-Security-Policy` (API: restrictive default-src/'none' or API-appropriate; FE via CloudFront)
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY` / `Frame-Ancestors 'none'`
- `Permissions-Policy` (disable unused browser features)
- `Cache-Control: no-store` on responses with PII or payment data
- Remove/omit `Server` / `X-Powered-By`

## Request hardening

- HTTPS only; reject or redirect HTTP at API Gateway / CloudFront.
- CORS **allowlist** (FE origin only); no `*`.
- Validate & sanitize **all** inputs (body, query, path); reject unknown fields when practical.
- Encode outputs; never reflect raw input into errors.
- Rate-limit / throttling on payment and write endpoints (API Gateway usage plans or equivalent).
- Idempotency keys on payment/create-transaction where applicable.
- Least-privilege IAM per microservice; no wildcard `*` on DynamoDB/secrets in prod.
- Uniform error body (no stack traces, no internal IDs leakage beyond correlationId).

## Checklist before merging an endpoint

OWASP-minded: injection, broken authz (if any), sensitive data exposure, misconfig (headers/CORS), SSRF on provider URLs (fixed base URL from env), logging/monitoring via shared logger, CSRF not applicable to token APIs but keep CORS tight.
